.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt LOADER.RPIBOOT 8 arm64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm loader.rpiboot
.Nd Raspberry Pi 5 kernel loader
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the
.Fx
loader for the Raspberry Pi 5, started directly by the board's VPU firmware
with no U-Boot and no EFI firmware in the boot path.
The firmware loads it from the FAT boot partition as though it were a Linux
arm64 kernel, as named by the
.Cm kernel
line of
.Pa config.txt ,
and enters it at exception level 2 with the MMU off and the physical address
of its device tree in register x0.
There is no EFI memory map; memory comes from the
.Pa /memory
node of that tree, which the firmware fills in.
.Pp
The console is the SoC PL011 UART on the three-pin debug connector, at
115200 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, as the firmware configured it.
The interpreter is
.Xr loader_simp 8 ,
which runs the commands in
.Pa /boot/loader.rc
and does not read
.Xr loader.conf 5 .
.Ss The initrd
.Nm
has no storage driver.
Its file system is the image the firmware loads into memory with the
.Pa config.txt
line
.Bd -literal -offset indent
initramfs <file> 0x30000000
.Ed
.Pp
The firmware records where it put the image in the
.Pa /chosen
node's
.Va linux,initrd-start
and
.Va linux,initrd-end
properties, and
.Nm
serves it as
.Li md0: ,
the current device.
It must be a bare UFS file system, such as
.Xr makefs 8
produces, and must start at or above 0x30000000, the end of the memory
.Nm
uses for itself and for assembling the kernel.
It must also end below the top of the first memory region, 0x3f400000.
.Pp
The kernel and its modules are loaded from that image.
Where the kernel's root file system is depends on
.Va rpiboot_initrd_root :
.Bl -tag -width "rpiboot_initrd_root"
.It Va rpiboot_initrd_root
When set to
.Dq YES ,
the whole image is copied behind the kernel as an
.Dq mfs_root
module just before the kernel is started, so
.Xr md 4
attaches it as
.Pa md0
and
.Va vfs.root.mountfrom Ns = Ns Dq ufs:/dev/md0
mounts it as root.
The Raspberry Pi 5 live system and installer run this way.
When unset, as on an installed system, the image carries only the kernel,
and the kernel mounts its root from wherever
.Va vfs.root.mountfrom
says.
.El
.Pp
An installed system's image is written by
.Xr rpi5-bootimg 8 .
.Ss Memory layout
.Bl -tag -width "0x10000000-0x30000000" -compact
.It 0x00200000
.Nm
itself
.It 0x04000000
device tree
.Pq Cm device_tree_address
.It 0x08000000
loader heap, 48 MiB
.It 0x10000000-0x30000000
kernel, modules and root image as they are assembled
.It 0x30000000
initrd
.El
.Ss Commands
In addition to the common loader commands,
.Nm
provides
.Ic reboot
and
.Ic poweroff ,
both through PSCI calls to the ARM Trusted Firmware.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/boot/rpiboot.bin" -compact
.It Pa /boot/rpiboot.bin
the loader, as installed; copied to the FAT boot partition
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr md 4 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr loader 8 ,
.Xr loader_simp 8 ,
.Xr rpi5-bootimg 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh BUGS
.Nm
cannot read the SD card, so an installed system's kernel has to be copied
into an image on the FAT partition after every change; see
.Xr rpi5-bootimg 8 .
